research/OSCR/2026-11-15-evaluation.md
OK research/OSCR/2026-11-15-evaluation.md Bear case=138 Bull case=93 decision=AVOID scorecard=6->3

- **What scores well:** returns, balance sheet and trend all score high. TTM ROIC is 33.8% and the price is 27.1% above its 200-day average after a +105.6% year.
- **What pulls it down:** I judged the moat as none and the key risk as high. The risk is ACA regulation (expired subsidies, 2027 income checks, the Columbus II lawsuit) on top of only one profitable year.
- **No entry price set:** I left it null because price is not the obstacle. The multiples are already low (P/E 11.7x against a peer median of 23.3x). A lower price would not fix the short profit record or the regulatory risk.
- **No fair value:** the fact sheet could not compute one, so the scenario targets are anchored to the 6-month low (bear), today's close (base) and the 52-week high (bull) instead.

I did not read the portfolio state, since it is only needed for a BUY. One trigger (members falling for two quarters in a row) has `"check": null` and another has no check field; the checker accepted both.
